          %p
            %br/
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Examples of sporadic (exceptional)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isogenies"} isogenies
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+groups"} spin groups
            onto orthogonal groups are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Garrett13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Garrett"}> Paul Garrett
              ,
              %em Sporadic isogenies to orthogonal groups
              (July 2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.umn.edu/~garrett/m/v/sporadic_isogenies.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Garrett-SporadicIsogenies.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            are listed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Abanov09
              %p
                Alexander Abanov, Homotopy groups of Lie groups 2009 (
                %a{:href => "http://felix.physics.sunysb.edu/~abanov/Teaching/Spring2009/Notes/abanov-cpA1-upload.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#MimuraToda63
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mamoru+Mimura"} Mamoru Mimura
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshi+Toda"} Hiroshi Toda
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Homotopy Groups of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi SU
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(3)
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 4
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(4)
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(2)
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.kjm/1250524818"} Euclid
            %li#Mimura67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mamoru+Mimura"}> Mamoru Mimura
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Homotopy groups of Lie groups of low rank
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.kjm/1250524375"} Euclid
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            of the manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(n)
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#MilnorStasheff74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Characteristic classes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691081229/characteristic-classes-am-76-volume-76"} ISBN:9780691081229
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/9781400881826"} doi:10.1515/9781400881826
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/milnstas.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Brown82
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+H.+Brown"}> Edgar H. Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The Cohomology of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi SO
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B SO_n
                    and
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi BO
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BO_n
                    with Integer Coefficients
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2044298"} jstor:2044298
            %li#Feshbach83
              %p
                Mark Feshbach,
                %em
                  The Integral Cohomology Rings of the Classifying Spaces of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{O}(n)
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SO
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SO}(n)
                Indiana Univ. Math. J. 32 (1983), 511-516 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1512/iumj.1983.32.32036"}> doi:10.1512/iumj.1983.32.32036
                )
            %li#Pittie91
              %p
                Harsh V. Pittie,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The integral homology and cohomology rings of SO(n) and Spin(n)
                = succeed "))" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(91)90108-E"} doi:10.1016/0022-4049(91)90108-E
            %li#RudolphSchmidt17
              %p
                Gerd Rudolph, Matthias Schmidt, around Theorem 4.2.23 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Geometry and Mathematical Physics: Part II. Fibre Bundles, Topology and Gauge Fields
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-94-024-0959-8"} doi:10.1007/978-94-024-0959-8
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#Tamura57
              Itiro Tamura,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Pontrjagin classes of homotopy types of manifolds
